# Files executed by a Linux shell or interpreter must keep LF in the working
# tree. This repository is cloned with core.autocrlf=true on Windows, which
# would otherwise rewrite them to CRLF, and the shebang then fails on Linux as
#   /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# Scoped deliberately to the affected files. A repository wide `* text=auto`
# would renormalise ~510 files and bury real changes in whitespace churn.
make-arch-pkg text eol=lf
make-deb-pkg  text eol=lf
make-rpm-pkg  text eol=lf
*.sh          text eol=lf
*.py          text eol=lf
*.desktop     text eol=lf
